  "summary": "When using the listen directive with the ssl parameter in the http block with TLSv1.3 enabled, an attacker can use a…",
  "details": "When using the listen directive with the ssl parameter in the http block with TLSv1.3 enabled, an attacker can use a specially crafted TLS connection to cause an infinite loop in the NGINX worker process while reading the HTTP request body. As a result, the worker process stops accepting new connections and processing existing connections. Note: Software versions which have reached End of Technical Support (EoTS) are not evaluated.\n\nImpact: This vulnerability allows a remote, unauthenticated attacker to cause a denial-of-service (DoS) of NGINX. There is no control plane exposure; this is a data plane issue only.\n\n\n\nNote: Software versions which have reached End of Technical Support (EoTS) are not evaluated.",
